{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2171-05-13 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this hospital stay. You’re here because of increasing pain and redness in your legs. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2171-05-13 13:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. My legs have been getting worse over the last two weeks. The right one started hurting and turning red, and now the left one has blisters and is draining fluid. I’ve been on IV antibiotics at home but it’s not helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2171-05-13 13:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve also been getting IV furosemide three times a week. Has the swelling improved?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2171-05-13 13:24:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not really. I stopped weighing myself because the numbers jump around so much. It’s frustrating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2171-05-13 13:25:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll monitor your weight here. Your labs show your white blood cell count is elevated, which can mean infection. But since the antibiotics aren’t working, we need to figure out if this is truly cellulitis or something else."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2171-05-13 13:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had cellulitis so many times. But this feels different. The blisters are new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2171-05-13 13:28:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. We’ll start you on IV vancomycin just in case, but we’ll also run some tests to rule out other causes. We’ve ordered a CT scan of your abdomen and pelvis to check for anything pressing on your veins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2171-05-13 13:29:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my breathing’s been okay, but I’ve had this cough and sinus pressure for a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2171-05-13 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your chest X-ray shows no pneumonia, so we think it’s from post-nasal drip. We’ll treat that separately. For now, we’re focusing on your legs and swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2171-05-14 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your CT scan came back. Good news — there’s no mass blocking your veins. That means your lymphedema isn’t being caused by a tumor or blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2171-05-14 09:17:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But why is it getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2171-05-14 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t have a full answer yet. The scan did show some small spots on your kidneys that weren’t there before. They’re not causing symptoms, but your primary doctor should follow up with an MRI to check them out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2171-05-14 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Spots on my kidneys? Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2171-05-14 09:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s too early to say. Most are benign, but we want to make sure. It’s something to discuss with your PCP after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2171-05-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat chest X-ray shows less fluid buildup than before. That’s a good sign. We’re also starting a diuretic drip to help with the swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2171-05-15 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help my legs feel better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2171-05-15 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hope so. But with lymphedema, fluid doesn’t respond as well to diuretics. We’re also restricting your fluids to 1.5 liters a day and keeping you on a very low-salt diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2171-05-16 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We consulted dermatology. They agree the redness may not be infection, but venous stasis from poor circulation. They recommend elevation, compression, and weight loss."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2171-05-16 08:47:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve tried compression pumps and wraps. Nothing works."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2171-05-16 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s been tough. Unna boots were suggested, but we don’t have them here. The key long-term goal is weight loss — it can make a big difference in lymphedema."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2171-05-17 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white blood cell count is still high, but it’s been chronically elevated for you. Blood cultures are negative — no bacteria in your blood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2171-05-17 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So is it not an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2171-05-17 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s looking less likely. Your exam hasn’t changed on antibiotics. We’d like to stop vancomycin and see how you do without it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2171-05-17 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, if you think that’s best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2171-05-18 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your echocardiogram shows your heart is pumping well. No heart failure. That’s good — it means your swelling isn’t from your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2171-05-18 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve always wondered if it was my heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2171-05-18 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, your heart looks strong. We also did a leg ultrasound — no blood clots. So we’re focusing on lymphedema and skin changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2171-05-19 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your kidney function is a concern. Creatinine went up from 1.1 to 1.4. We’ve stopped the IV diuretic drip to protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2171-05-19 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is my kidney damaged?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2171-05-19 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a temporary change, likely from the diuretics. We’ll monitor it. You’ll go back to oral bumetanide at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2171-05-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also treating your sinus infection with levofloxacin. You’ve had purulent discharge for two weeks — this should help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2171-05-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My nose has been bleeding a little. Is that from the nasal spray?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2171-05-20 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, fluticasone can cause that. We’ve stopped it. The antibiotic should still help your sinuses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2171-05-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR was low at 1.7, so we increased your warfarin to 8.5 mg daily. Your latest INR is 2.0 — that’s in the safe range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2171-05-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still on blood thinners for my past clots?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2171-05-21 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because of your history of DVT and pulmonary embolism. You’ll continue 8.5 mg daily. Your PCP will check your INR soon after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2171-05-22 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had a brief episode where you were unresponsive for a few minutes. Was that a seizure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2171-05-22 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I think so. I get those sometimes, but the last real one was a while ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2171-05-22 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your prolactin level was normal afterward, which suggests it might not have been an epileptic seizure. Neurology thinks it could be a non-epileptic event."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2171-05-22 08:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So not a real seizure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2171-05-22 08:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s hard to say without an EEG, but it’s possible. We’ll keep you on your seizure meds just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2171-05-23 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your leg redness is still there, but we’re confident it’s not infection. We’re discharging you on nystatin for oral thrush and finishing the levofloxacin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2171-05-23 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my legs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2171-05-23 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll restart bumetanide and spironolactone. Continue elevation and low salt. Your weight is 161.5 kg — only a small change, but that’s expected with lymphedema."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2171-05-24 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge plan. You’ll go home with services. Your PCP will manage your follow-up labs and the kidney MRI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2171-05-24 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous about managing everything at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2171-05-24 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve arranged home health to help. And weigh yourself every morning — call if you gain more than 3 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2171-05-25 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing — the CT also showed fatty liver. It’s common with obesity and not urgent, but weight loss helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2171-05-25 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It always comes back to weight, doesn’t it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2171-05-25 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s hard. But even modest loss can improve your swelling and overall health."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2171-05-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. Creatinine is 1.4, WBC is down a bit. You’re doing well for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2171-05-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still have some drainage from my left leg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2171-05-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s serous fluid, not pus. It’s from the skin changes, not infection. Keep the area clean and dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2171-05-26 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my cough?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2171-05-26 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still from post-nasal drip. It should improve as your sinuses clear. Use benzonatate if it bothers you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Final instructions: finish levofloxacin, continue nystatin, restart bumetanide, and follow up with your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the kidney spots?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your PCP will order the MRI. Don’t worry — it’s a precaution. Also, keep using nicotine patches if you’re trying to cut back on smoking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m not ready to quit yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay. We support whatever step you’re ready to take. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll send all the details to your primary care team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make that appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. And remember — elevation, low salt, and daily weights. You’ve made it through another tough episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2171-05-27 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2171-05-13 13:20:00",
    "admission_end": "2171-05-27 17:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 58-year-old woman was admitted for worsening bilateral leg pain, redness, and swelling, initially concerning for cellulitis, but found to be due to chronic lymphedema with venous stasis changes. Despite prior outpatient treatment with IV furosemide and clindamycin, her symptoms progressed, prompting hospitalization for diuresis and infection evaluation. IV vancomycin was started but discontinued after no improvement and negative blood cultures, with dermatology attributing findings to stasis. A CT scan ruled out abdominal masses but revealed new renal lesions requiring outpatient MRI follow-up. Diuresis with IV furosemide and metolazone was limited by rising creatinine, leading to discontinuation. She was treated for sinusitis with levofloxacin and oral thrush with nystatin. Her INR was optimized on warfarin, and a brief non-epileptic event was noted. She was discharged home with services on oral diuretics, with instructions to monitor weight, follow up with her PCP, and complete imaging for renal lesions.",
    "problems": [
      "Lymphedema, not elsewhere classified",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Candidal stomatitis",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 50.0-59.9, adult",
      "Morbid (severe) obesity due to excess calories",
      "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, unspecified",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, not intractable, without status epilepticus",
      "Postnasal drip",
      "Acute upper respiratory infection, unspecified",
      "Epistaxis",
      "Chronic maxillary sinusitis",
      "Fibromyalgia",
      "Benign neoplasm of left adrenal gland",
      "Other specified disorders of kidney and ureter",
      "Nicotine dependence, unspecified, uncomplicated",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Personal history of other venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Long term (current) use of anticoagulants",
